! Part 2 — same board, same key, one character of policy changed
! The policy now reads  gate=measure-before-unsea1  (the last character is a digit 1, not an L)
$SEALED -p $PORT status
: pause 0.8
! The measurement moved. The sealed value did not, because the seal lives in the keystore, not in the image.
$SEALED -p $PORT sign --tx tx.bin
: pause 0.8
! That is the whole idea: no network, no vendor, no "please don't". The key is not released.
$SEALED -p $PORT status
: pause 1.0
